      <description>Tesla’s cybercab is, in one sense, the ideal product. Here is a nominally autonomous vehicle that works, up to a point, in a bare sliver of the US; it can be rendered inoperable by Tesla Inc. if you do something deemed “improper”; and can’t be used to earn money as a robotaxi without Tesla’s permission. You aren’t allowed to resell your cybercab or modify it, even the gold paint job, and Tesla can collect video footage of whatever you’re doing in the car. Plus, the cybercab lacks a steering whee</description>
